---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "interdisciplinary thinking — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>interdisciplinary thinking</h1>
    <p>interdisciplinary work happens at the intersection of fields. a product designer needs psychology + engineering + economics. an epidemiologist needs biology + statistics + social dynamics. the magic happens when you integrate, not just layer.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>identify the core question you're trying to solve</li>
      <li>map which disciplines touch that question</li>
      <li>learn just enough of each field to spot insights, not to become an expert</li>
      <li>find practitioners in each field and ask them what they'd see</li>
      <li>integrate ideas; don't just list them side-by-side</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="try">pick a problem you care about. list three disciplines that might inform it. spend time in each, then synthesize.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
